 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Input",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Pins 1 and 2 drive two infrared emitters connected anti-parallel. Current in one direction lights one emitter and current in the other direction lights the second, so the input accepts AC or either DC polarity, and each emitter protects the other against reverse voltage. The forward current rating, ±40 mA, and the test conditions are given for either polarity."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output and base pin",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "The output is an NPN phototransistor with collector, emitter and base on separate pins. A resistor from base to emitter lowers the transfer ratio, the more so the lower the input current: at VCE = 0.3 V and 10 mA input the ratio is about half its open-base value with about 70 kΩ, and falls to nothing near 20 kΩ. The same resistor shortens turn-off, to about 0.15 of the open-base turn-off time at 100 kΩ, while turn-on time peaks near 2 MΩ at about twice its open-base value."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Transfer ratio",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "The current transfer ratio is highest near 15 mA input and falls off on both sides; at 1 mA it is about half the 10 mA figure. It also falls with rising temperature, to about 0.68 of its 25 °C value at 110 °C for 10 mA input."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Switching",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "Switching times are taken with the collector pulled up through RL to VCC and the output read at the collector, on a 5 V output swing with 90 % and 10 % levels. ton runs from the input's rising edge to the output falling through 10 %, and tr is the output's fall from 90 % to 10 %; toff runs from the input's falling edge to the output rising through 90 %, and tf is the output's rise from 10 % to 90 %. With IF = 10 mA and VCC = 10 V, toff and tf grow roughly in proportion to RL above 1 kΩ, to about 260 µs and 180 µs at 10 kΩ, while ton and tr stay between about 2.5 and 8.5 µs."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Marking",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "The first line of the top marking is H11AA1, followed by X on option 1 parts; the second line carries V, the year-and-week date code YWW and 24. The T reel suffix is not marked. A dot marks pin 1."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Soldering",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The leads can take 260 °C for 10 s."
  }
 ],
